1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://sok.riksarkivet.se/SBL/Presentation.aspx?id=7565
2 CONT
2 CONT http://runeberg.org/vemarvem/skane66/0714.html
2 CONT
2 CONT * Made a legal name change from Andersson to Rausing.
2 CONT * See [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ruben_Rausing '''Wikipedia...''']
2 CONT
2 CONT Ruben Rausing (17 June 1895 – 8 October 1983) was the founder of the liquid food packaging company Tetra Pak. He was born in Helsingborg, Sweden in 1895.
2 CONT
2 CONT Contents  [show]  Early life[edit] Ruben Rausing was born in 1895 in Råå, a small fishing hamlet in the district of Raus outside of Helsingborg in the south of Sweden, to August and Mathilda Andersson. His father ran a small but s
2 CONC uccessful business as a master painter.[1] Rausing went to Upper Secondary School in Helsingborg, graduating in 1915.[2] When doing his military service, Rausing, at the time still called Ruben Andersson, was allegedly nicknamed r
2 CONC ausingen by his fellow servicemen, meaning "the lad from Raus".[3] Taking a liking to this name, he eventually changed his surname from Andersson to Rausing.
2 CONT
2 CONT Career[edit] With the help of a loan from his aunt, Rausing studied at the recently founded Stockholm School of Economics and Business Administration, graduating in 1918.[4][5] After a brief engagement at the privately owned Enski
2 CONC lda Banken, Rausing was employed by Sveriges Litografiska Tryckerier, SLT (later renamed Esselte), a well-known printing company. In 1919 he earned a scholarship from SSE to continue his studies at Columbia University in New York 
2 CONC and obtained a MSc in Economics in 1920.[6][7] Experiencing self-service grocery stores for the first time during his stay in America, Rausing realised that this system, yet unknown in Europe, was going to be part of a new way of 
2 CONC retailing.[8][9]
2 CONT
2 CONT Returning to Sweden in 1920, Rausing continued his employment at SLT, first as a Manager Assistant and then as a Manager. During his time at SLT, Rausing became closely aqcuainted with the industrialist Erik Åkerlund and in 1929 R
2 CONC ausing left SLT to form a new packaging company together with Åkerlund in Malmö, Åkerlund & Rausing. Åkerlund & Rausing was the first packaging company in Scandinavia and eventually became a leading manufacturer of dry food carton
2 CONC  packages.[10][11] Initially, however, the company had difficulties making profits and in 1933 Åkerlund sold his share to Rausing, who became the sole owner.[12]
2 CONT
2 CONT At the time, non-carbonated drinks such as milk and juices were sold in heavy and cumbersome glass bottles and Rausing was determined to find a way of implementing the new, modern packaging technology, spending a lot of resources 
2 CONC on developing new concepts.[13] With the aim of producing a carton container for liquid foods, similar to the hygienic and practical wax-coated paper cartons Rausing had seen overseas, Åkerlund & Rausing created the plastic-coated
2 CONC  carton tetrahedron, patented on 27 March 1944.[14][15]
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1951 there was still no viable packaging material for the new package, and efforts to develop packaging material increased.[16] Finally, in 1952, the first machine producing tetrahedron cream packages was sold to Lundabygdens M
2 CONC ejeri, a local dairy.[17] The new packaging system was not an immediate success and the company had difficulties throughout the 1950s, with Rausing continuing to spend large amounts on development. Initially catering primarily to 
2 CONC the Swedish market, the company expanded gradually, with Germany (1954), France (1954) and Italy (1956) as its first export markets.[18]
2 CONT
2 CONT Tetra Pak's commercial break-through did not arrive until the mid-60s with the new Tetra Brik package, introduced in 1963, and the development of the Aseptic technology.[19] The late 1960s and the 1970s saw a global expansion of t
2 CONC he company, much due to the new Tetra Brik Aseptic package, debuted in 1968, which opened up new markets in the developing world and sparked off a virtual explosion in sales.[20] After 30 years of ceaseless effort and investment, 
2 CONC Rausing's venture finally proved to be successful and Tetra Pak eventually became the leading food processing and packaging company in the world.[21]
2 CONT
2 CONT Honours[edit] Rausing was made Doctor Honoris Causa in Medicine at Lund University in 1957, in Economics at the Stockholm School of Economics and Business Administration in 1959 and in Technology at the Royal Institute of Technolo
2 CONC gy in 1977.[22][23] He was a member of the Royal Swedish Academy of Engineering Sciences (Ingenjörsvetenskapsakademin, IVA).
2 CONT
2 CONT Personal life[edit] Ruben Rausing was married to Elisabeth (née Varenius) and had three sons, Hans, Gad and Sven. For tax reasons, Rausing left Sweden for Rome in 1969. All his life, however, he kept his country home Simontorp, ou
2 CONC tside of Lund.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ruben_Rausing
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
